==Trivia==
*Little Leaguer Cat's name in the Japanese version, Kyuji Cat, is likely a reference to famed baseballer [[wikipedia:Kyuji Fujikawa|Kyuji Fujikawa]]. It could also be a pun, as 球児 (Kyū Ji) literally translates to 'ball child', and Little Leaguer Cat is a child who likes to play ball.
*Major Leaguer Cat's Barrier Breaker ability was added in [[Version 7.2 Update|Version 7.2]].
*Golfer Cat appears to be a reference to an old, classic manga: ''There's Good Weather Tomorrow'', otherwise known as Ashita Tenki ni Nāre, as he greatly resembles the main protagonist in design. This reference is also present in the combo [[Clear Skies (Combo)|Clear Skies]], as that combo's name in the Japanese version is literally あした天気になーれ (Ashita Tenki ni Nāre).

